# Rust
target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
.cargo/*
!.cargo/audit.toml

# Cargo lock files: track the workspace-root Cargo.lock (CI's setup:rust runs
# `cargo fetch --locked` and `Dockerfile` copies it), but ignore lock files
# inside the workspace-excluded sub-projects, which each have their own
# independent dep tree.
#
# EXCEPTION: deposit-prover/Cargo.lock IS tracked. The deposit circuit's
# verifying key (and the VkBlob embedded in the on-chain USDCBridge) is a
# deterministic function of the full dependency closure, so the lock must be
# pinned for the VK to be reproducible. An untracked lock here is exactly what
# made the original on-chain VK (147efe14…) unbuildable after transitive drift.
# See docs/deposit_vk_reproducibility.md.
poseidon-proof/Cargo.lock
crates/bridge-snark-utils/Cargo.lock
crates/bridge-relayer-daemon/Cargo.lock

# Foundry / Solidity
contracts/ethereum/out/
contracts/ethereum/cache/
contracts/ethereum/broadcast/
contracts/ethereum/lib/

# Environment variables and secrets
.env
.env.local
.env.production
.env.*.local
.env.shellnet
.env.sepolia
.secrets

